Chapter: BritainWindow

 Britain's walk window is the union of three measured extents, one walkable tile beyond the outermost walls, rounded out
 to whole 8 by 8 map blocks, which is what the map cache fills (wmc-fill, wmc-aligned). Walls are
 the TILEDATA wall-flagged (0x10) statics of the 1.25 client's STATICS0.MUL (measured 2026-10-09). The town: x 1360 to
 1519, y 1488 to 1752, the docks' fish market included (the eastern Oaken Oar's south wall is y 1751, UOAIX-167). Castle Britain: the wall ring through the east gatehouse at 1399,1623, corner towers at
 1295,1559 and 1407,1695. The unsigned houses east of the town (UOAIX-163): the last wall east of Britain stands at
 x 1711, y 1551, and none stands from x 1712 to 1800.

  bwn-town-x1 : Integer = 1360
  bwn-town-y1 : Integer = 1488
  bwn-town-x2 : Integer = 1519
  bwn-town-y2 : Integer = 1752
  bwn-castle-x1 : Integer = 1295
  bwn-castle-y1 : Integer = 1559
  bwn-castle-x2 : Integer = 1407
  bwn-castle-y2 : Integer = 1695
  bwn-east-x2 : Integer = 1711
  bwn-x1 : Integer = ((if bwn-castle-x1 < bwn-town-x1 then bwn-castle-x1 else bwn-town-x1) - 1) / 8 * 8
  bwn-y1 : Integer = (if bwn-castle-y1 - 1 < bwn-town-y1 then bwn-castle-y1 - 1 else bwn-town-y1) / 8 * 8
  bwn-x2 : Integer = ((if bwn-east-x2 > bwn-town-x2 then bwn-east-x2 else bwn-town-x2) + 1 + 8) / 8 * 8 - 1
  bwn-y2 : Integer = ((if bwn-castle-y2 + 1 > bwn-town-y2 then bwn-castle-y2 + 1 else bwn-town-y2) + 8) / 8 * 8 - 1
  bwn-width : Integer = bwn-x2 - bwn-x1 + 1
  bwn-height : Integer = bwn-y2 - bwn-y1 + 1
